ar confound: importance scores degraded by the very pruning they're composed with\n2. Failed mitigation: if oracle boundaries don't work, is phase-aware allocation viable at all?\n3. GSM8K specificity attenuation: only one clean cross-benchmark replication\n4. Placeholder sections in actual paper\n5. \"Emergent\" vs \"modulated\" terminology\n\n## Your Task\nReact to R2's review. For each of R2's major points:\n1. State whether you AGREE, PARTIALLY AGREE, or DISAGREE\n2. Provide brief justification\n3. Note any points where R2's review changes your own assessment\n\nThen provide:\n- Your revised overall score (if changed) with justification\n- Top 3 most important issues for the paper, synthesizing both reviews\n- Whether you think this paper should be accepted at a top venue (~25% acceptance rate)\n\nKeep response under 800 words.","uuid":"1d02c5f3-ba46-4bef-840d-172636b08d6e","session_id":"813b3e7b-de85-4f91-a594-365a71c45c1e"}
