{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0142ko7mqEJDz1dy9uSac1fb","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_11/projects/phase-gated-compound-sparse/decisions.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"_next_id: 99\\\\ndecisions:\\\\n- id: D001\\\\n  date: 2026-05-13 17:44 UTC\\\\n  summary: MVP 方案：用 Interaction Index 跨 phase 差异验证核心假设\\\\n  rationale: 评审建议 novelty 锚定在 \\\\\\\"phase-dependent interaction direction reversal\\\\\\\"。MVP\\\\n    聚焦验证这一点：在 MATH-500 子集上 profiling DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B，用 ThinKV 方法切分 phases，计算\\\\n    attention × KV 的 Interaction Index。比全 grid search 更聚焦，直接验证核心 novelty 锚点。Pass =\\\\n    II 跨 phase 显著不同；Fail = II 恒定。预计 10-15 H100-hours。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on: []\\\\n- id: D002\\\\n  date: 2026-05-13 17:48 UTC\\\\n  summary: 向 Manager 申请 4×H100-80GB 租卡，预计 8-10 天，¥3200-5000\\\\n  rationale: 12 天截稿，4 GPU 并行可将日历时间压到 ~8 天（留 4 天 buffer）。2 GPU 需 11 天，buffer 不足 1 天，风险过高。用户明确授权\\\\\\\"几张都可以\\\\\\\"。GPU\\\\n    就绪 hard deadline 5/14 EOD。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D001\\\\n- id: D003\\\\n  date: 2026-05-13 17:54 UTC\\\\n  summary: Throughput 策略：RTX 6000 Pro 做开发/accuracy，最终 throughput 短租 H100\\\\n  rationale: IDEA_BRIEF 硬约束要求\\\\\\\"Report wall-clock and throughput on H100\\\\\\\"，baseline 论文（Polar\\\\n    Sparsity、SeerAttention-R）均报告 H100 数字。RTX 6000 Pro (sm_89) vs H100 (sm_90) 的 kernel\\\\n    speedup 可能不同。策略(a)：RTX 6000 Pro 做全部开发+accuracy+ablation（硬件无关），仅 throughput 基准测试短租\\\\n    H100 ~2-4h（~$6-12）。比策略(b)全在 RTX 6000 Pro 上报告更有说服力，成本极低。H100 在 M5 阶段再申请。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D002\\\\n- id: D004\\\\n  date: 2026-05-13 17:58 UTC\\\\n  summary: Throughput benchmark 硬件从 H100 改为 H20（Hopper sm_90，用户确认无 H100 可用）\\\\n  rationale: H20 与 H100 同为 Hopper sm_90，kernel 兼容无需额外适配。96GB HBM3 + 4TB/s 带宽适合 inference\\\\n    benchmark。在 H20 上重跑所有 baseline 确保公平比较，报告 relative speedup ratio（Hopper 架构内比值稳定）。H100\\\\n    不可用，H20 是最佳替代。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D003\\\\n- id: D005\\\\n  date: 2026-05-13 18:01 UTC\\\\n  summary: GPU 从 4× RTX 6000 Pro 换为 4× H20-NVLink 96GB\\\\n  rationale: H20 是 Hopper sm_90（与 H100 同架构），kernel 无需跨架构适配。4TB/s HBM3 带宽远优于 RTX 6000\\\\n    Pro（~960GB/s），7B 推理速度接近 H100。全程同架构消除 M5+ 短租需求，简化流程。用户主动提出可换 H20。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D004\\\\n- id: D006\\\\n  date: 2026-05-13 18:40 UTC\\\\n  summary: GPU 实际为 Blackwell sm_100+（非 Ada sm_89）：MVP 不阻塞，kernel/throughput 阶段需 Hopper\\\\n  rationale: nvidia-smi 显示 \\\\\\\"RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell Server Edition\\\\\\\" compute cap 12.0。MVP\\\\n    profiling 仅需 PyTorch forward pass 无架构依赖。M4 kernel integration 阶段 Triton/TileLang\\\\n    对 sm_100+ 支持待验证。M5+ throughput benchmark 仍需 Hopper 架构（H20）做可比测量。先用 Blackwell 推进\\\\n    M1-M3，不阻塞。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D005\\\\n- id: D007\\\\n  date: 2026-05-13 20:20 UTC\\\\n  summary: M1 结果无效（KV bug + KDE 失败）：两路并行——P0 修复重跑 + 替代 segmentation 开发\\\\n  rationale: KV eviction 的 per-layer mask 交集 bug 导致全 NaN（P0），KDE 82% 样本找不到 tri-modal\\\\n    结构（P1）。但积极信号存在：execution phase 对 head pruning 敏感度 474× vs reasoning 14×，说明 token\\\\n    级结构性差异真实存在。决策：(A) P0 修复后重跑 M1 获取有效 II + 诊断数据，(B) 并行开发 GMM+BIC / quantile-based\\\\n    / multi-layer 替代 segmentation。先看重跑 II 是否在现有 3 phase 间有差异，差异显著则 KDE 虽粗糙但假设成立；无差异则上替代方案。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_interaction_index_profiling\\\\n    role: failed_run\\\\n    result: KV NaN + KDE 82% fallback + 90% transition\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D001\\\\n- id: D008\\\\n  date: 2026-05-13 21:23 UTC\\\\n  summary: M1v2 假设未获支持但测量方法有问题——M1v3 最后诊断：降 sparsity + quantile segmentation + NaN\\\\n    guard\\\\n  rationale: M1v2 所有 phase 均 super-additive、无 sign reversal，但 3 个方法论问题使结论不可靠：(1) 30%\\\\n    random masking 导致 24-33× PPL 退化，超出安全区；(2) KDE 90% fallback，phase 划分无意义；(3) NaN\\\\n    CI artifact 导致虚假 PASS。M1v3 修复这三点后做最终判定。叙事 pivot：即使全 super-additive，magnitude 跨\\\\n    segment 差异（+17.8 vs +3.1）仍支持 phase-aware allocation。Pass = magnitude CI 不重叠；Fail\\\\n    = magnitude 无差异。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_ii_profiling_v2\\\\n    role: diagnostic\\\\n    result: All super-additive, no sign reversal, NaN artifact PASS, KDE 90% fallback\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D007\\\\n- id: D009\\\\n  date: 2026-05-13 22:44 UTC\\\\n  summary: Random masking 系统性混淆——v1-v3 测了错误条件；importance-based masking 是正确 MVP 测试，立即启动\\\\n    v4\\\\n  rationale: 三次 MVP 实验全用 random masking（torch.randperm 选 heads/KV），天然产生 super-additive\\\\n    interaction（随机移除组件造成相关性损伤）。初步 importance-vs-random 对比已显示 masking 方法是 II 符号的主导因子（importance\\\\n    II=-0.91 sub-additive vs random II=+9.38 super-additive）。v3 在 clean methodology\\\\n    下仍全 super-additive 是预期结果，不代表 PACS 假设无效。真正的 MVP 判定需在 importance-based masking 条件下测试\\\\n    per-phase II——这才是实际部署条件下的 compound sparsity 行为。v3 high vs mid 在 s=0.2 下 CI 几乎不重叠（[1.06,3.55]\\\\n    vs [-1.06,1.30]），暗示 importance-based 下 magnitude 差异可能更显著。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_ii_profiling_v3\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: negative under random masking, but confirms methodology is sound\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_ii_profiling_v2\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: negative, methodology issues identified and fixed in v3\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_interaction_index_profiling\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: failed (bugs), but importance-vs-random preliminary data is key signal\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D008\\\\n- id: D010\\\\n  date: 2026-05-13 22:44 UTC\\\\n  summary: MVP FAIL on phase-dependent reversal; PIVOT to strategy-dependent direction\\\\n    reversal as core novelty\\\\n  rationale: 三轮 MVP 实验（v1 bug/v2 negative/v3 negative）确认 phase-dependent direction\\\\n    reversal 不存在——所有 phase 均 super-additive，v2 的 5.8x magnitude 差异是 KDE 不均衡 artifact。但\\\\n    importance vs random masking 数据发现 strategy-dependent direction reversal：random\\\\n    30% II=+9.38（super-additive）vs importance 30% II=-0.91（sub-additive），20% 也有符号反转。这是更干净、更强的\\\\n    novelty 锚点，直接 motivate learned compound controller。Pivot 方向：以 strategy-dependent\\\\n    interaction reversal 为核心 claim，phase conditioning 降为可选的二级贡献。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_interaction_index_profiling\\\\n    role: initial MVP (bugged)\\\\n    result: failed\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_ii_profiling_v2\\\\n    role: P0 fix rerun\\\\n    result: negative - no direction reversal\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_ii_profiling_v3\\\\n    role: low sparsity + quantile segmentation\\\\n    result: negative - no magnitude difference\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D008\\\\n  - D007\\\\n  - D001\\\\n- id: D011\\\\n  date: 2026-05-14 01:00 UTC\\\\n  summary: Float16 NaN→II bias discovered at s≥0.3; fix to float32 forward, don't\\\\n    pause running batch\\\\n  rationale: Agent 发现 head masking hook 中 inf×0→NaN 导致高 sparsity 下 both_ppl 为 NaN，II\\\\n    聚合排除这些 segment 造成系统性偏差。当前 batch (s025/s035/v4d) 保持运行作为 float16 reference，并行实施\\\\n    float32 修复，完成后重跑。Random masking 不受影响。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_v4_legacy_s035\\\\n    role: affected\\\\n    result: running, float16 results may be biased\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_ii_profiling_v4d\\\\n    role: affected\\\\n    result: running, float16 results may be biased\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_v4_legacy_s025\\\\n    role: reference\\\\n    result: running, likely unaffected at s=0.25\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_v4_random_r2\\\\n    role: control\\\\n    result: running, unaffected by this bug\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D010\\\\n- id: D012\\\\n  date: 2026-05-14 01:07 UTC\\\\n  summary: 暂停 importance-based 实验规划，紧急审查 KV importance metric 正确性\\\\n  rationale: 'Reviewer 发现 importance-based KV eviction 的 PPL 退化比 random eviction 严重\\\\n    26-60 倍（s=0.3: 408.98 vs 6.77），完全反直觉。cumulative_attention_received 作为 importance\\\\n    proxy 可能失效或排序方向有 bug。如果 metric 是坏的，D010 的 strategy-dependent direction reversal\\\\n    是 artifact 而非真实现象，整个 importance-based 路线需要重新评估。'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_v4_random_r2\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: random baseline 全 super-additive，数据可靠\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_v4a_r2\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: importance-based kv_ppl 异常高，26-60x worse than random\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D010\\\\n- id: D013\\\\n  date: 2026-05-14 01:16 UTC\\\\n  summary: 暂停 importance masking 结论，根因确认：cumulative_attention_received 有因果注意力位置偏差，驱逐最近上下文导致灾难性退化\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 根因分析确认：causal attention 中 position 0 被 N-1 个 token 关注（累积最高），position\\\\n    N-1 仅被自身关注（累积最低）。topk(largest=False) 驱逐最低分 = 驱逐最新位置 = 破坏最近上下文。这解释了 importance\\\\n    eviction 比 random 差 26-60× 的现象。s025 的 II per-sample mean (+152.7) 与聚合计算 (-107.6)\\\\n    符号相反，CI 宽 455 单位，统计意义为零。D010 的 strategy-dependent direction reversal 可能完全是坏指标伪影。修复方向：position\\\\n    normalization importance[j] /= (seq_len - j)。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_v4_legacy_s025\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: II=+152.7 但聚合计算=-107.6，符号矛盾\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_v4_legacy_s035\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: II=-462.7, CI=[-1557,+101]，极不稳定\\\\n  - exp\\\\n\\\\n... [截断: 省略 65052 字符，传 max_chars=0 获取完整内容]\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 73052, \\\"truncated\\\": true}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01CcbP9s7iFcGqm9KuZ1ESxf","session_id":"813b3e7b-de85-4f91-a594-365a71c45c1e","uuid":"acf08dda-4043-4178-8112-8627887c6229","timestamp":"2026-05-16T08:09:36.132Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AyVa8whnXNdamYYmQni1by","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NH1j4MdiikGSySZVjUDam8","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2 reacts to R1's review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 2 (R2). You previously reviewed the paper \"Phase-Gated Compound Sparsity\" focusing on Novelty and Related Work. Your scores were:\n- Novelty: 3\n- Related Work Completeness: 4\n- Significance/Impact: 3\n- Framing/Claims: 3\n- Overall: 3\n\nNow you have received Reviewer 1's (R1) review, which focused on Methods and Experiments. R1's scores were:\n- Methodological Soundness: 4\n- Experimental Rigor: 3\n- Statistical Claims: 3\n- Completeness: 4\n- Overall: 3.5\n\n## R1's Key Points:\n\n**Statistical inflation:**\n- Spearman ρ=1.0 with only 4 data points is trivially achieved by any monotonic sequence (1/24 = 4.2% by chance). Used as headline result throughout but statistically uninformative.\n- Cross-model Pearson r=0.85 with 8 non-independent data points (4 from DS, 4 from QW) — nested structure not accounted for, wide CI [0.40, 0.97]\n- Bonferroni k=4 is appropriate but total test count and BH-FDR not mentioned in dream paper\n\n**Experimental gaps:**\n- Model diversity insufficient: 2/3 models share Qwen2 architecture; LLaMA shows 60% weaker effect\n- No baselines beyond random eviction (no recency-based, sliding-window, learned policies)\n- Sparsity range 0.15-0.30 is narrow; practitioners use s>0.50\n- GPQA n=50 is underpowered per the paper's own analysis\n- H2O confound (head pruning alters scores used for importance eviction) omitted from dream paper\n\n**Missing ablations:**\n- No ablation on head pruning criterion\n- No ablation on KV cache budget (independent of s)\n- No ablation on decoding strategy (greedy only)\n\n**Strengths R1 acknowledged:**\n- Well-designed factorial experiment\n- Principled II metric (additive null + multiplicative verification)\n- Phase segmentation validation against <think> tokens (κ=0.88)\n- Thorough robustness checks in actual paper\n- Honest negative result reporting in actual paper\n- Language switching as creative behavioral probe\n\n**R1's Questions:**\n1. Spearman ρ=1.0 should be replaced by Jonckheere-Terpstra as primary evidence\n2. H2O confound: test eviction with scores independent of pruned heads\n3. Gini-II mechanism mismatch: both strategies show similar Gini drops but 15-17x severity divergence\n4. Practical deployment at s>0.30?\n5. LLaMA n=250 vs actual n=49 discrepancy\n\n## Your Task\nReact to R1's review. For each of R1's major points:\n1. State whether you AGREE, PARTIALLY AGREE, or DISAGREE\n2. Provide brief justification\n3. Note any points where R1's review changes your own assessment\n\nThen provide:\n- Your revised overall score (if changed) with justification\n- Top 3 most important issues for the paper, synthesizing both reviews\n- Whether you think this paper should be accepted at a top venue (~25% acceptance rate)\n\nKeep response under 800 words.","model":"opus"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11875,"cache_read_input_tokens":52937,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11875},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"813b3e7b-de85-4f91-a594-365a71c45c1e","uuid":"2887a67c-12e7-4389-aeb3-2825211df829"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"ab00c90528b8d6f26","tool_use_id":"toolu_01NH1j4MdiikGSySZVjUDam8","description":"R2 reacts to R1's review","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are Reviewer 2 (R2). You previously reviewed the paper \"Phase-Gated Compound Sparsity\" focusing on Novelty and Related Work. Your scores were:\n- Novelty: 3\n- Related Work Completeness: 4\n- Significance/Impact: 3\n- Framing/Claims: 3\n- Overall: 3\n\nNow you have received Reviewer 1's (R1) review, which focused on Methods and Experiments. R1's scores were:\n- Methodological Soundness: 4\n- Experimental Rigor: 3\n- Statistical Claims: 3\n- Completeness: 4\n- Overall: 3.5\n\n## R1's Key Points:\n\n**Statistical inflation:**\n- Spearman ρ=1.0 with only 4 data points is trivially achieved by any monotonic sequence (1/24 = 4.2% by chance). Used as headline result throughout but statistically uninformative.\n- Cross-model Pearson r=0.85 with 8 non-independent data points (4 from DS, 4 from QW) — nested structure not accounted for, wide CI [0.40, 0.97]\n- Bonferroni k=4 is appropriate but total test count and BH-FDR not mentioned in dream paper\n\n**Experimental gaps:**\n- Model diversity insufficient: 2/3 models share Qwen2 architecture; LLaMA shows 60% weaker effect\n- No baselines beyond random eviction (no recency-based, sliding-window, learned policies)\n- Sparsity range 0.15-0.30 is narrow; practitioners use s>0.50\n- GPQA n=50 is underpowered per the paper's own analysis\n- H2O confound (head pruning alters scores used for importance eviction) omitted from dream paper\n\n**Missing ablations:**\n- No ablation on head pruning criterion\n- No ablation on KV cache budget (independent of s)\n- No ablation on decoding strategy (greedy only)\n\n**Strengths R1 acknowledged:**\n- Well-designed factorial experiment\n- Principled II metric (additive null + multiplicative verification)\n- Phase segmentation validation against <think> tokens (κ=0.88)\n- Thorough robustness checks in actual paper\n- Honest negative result reporting in actual paper\n- Language switching as creative behavioral probe\n\n**R1's Questions:**\n1. Spearman ρ=1.0 should be replaced by Jonckheere-Terpstra as primary evidence\n2. H2O confound: test eviction with scores independent of pruned heads\n3. Gini-II mechanism mismatch: both strategies show similar Gini drops but 15-17x severity divergence\n4. Practical deployment at s>0.30?\n5. LLaMA n=250 vs actual n=49 discrepancy\n\n## Your Task\nReact to R1's review. For each of R1's major points:\n1. State whether you AGREE, PARTIALLY AGREE, or DISAGREE\n2. Provide brief justification\n3. Note any points where R1's review changes your own assessment\n\nThen provide:\n- Your revised overall score (if changed) with justification\n- Top 3 most important issues for the paper, synthesizing both reviews\n- Whether you think this paper should be accepted at a top venue (~25% acceptance rate)\n\nKeep response under 800 words.","uuid":"c31e1950-2551-4c49-9b19-659a5d602b00","session_id":"813b3e7b-de85-4f91-a594-365a71c45c1e"}
